  "body": "Found by the in-house qualification run of 2026-10-18 on the AX7101 (dev e9cbb676, processor 2cbed0a9).\n\n**Behaviour.**\n- On LOCK_ENTITY with the UNLOCK flag, the solicited response echoes flags = UNLOCK (1).\n- The unsolicited notification to the other registered controllers carries flags 0.\n- locked_id is 0 in both.\n\n**Required.**\n- IEEE 1722.1-2021 7.5.2: \"An unsolicited notification is sent by using an unsolicited response to the command\".\n- 7.4.2.1: the response carries the command's flags (Table 7-143).\n- Milan v1.2 5.4.5.1 says only that the notifications carry the same information. Where Milan is silent, IEEE 1722.1-2021 decides.\n\n**Source.** `hdl/aecp/ucode/gen_ucode.py:1104-1118` (E_LOCKUNS) reports the current state with flags 0, by design.\n\n**Done when:**\n- the notification driven by a LOCK_ENTITY command echoes the command's flags, as the response does;\n- the lock-timeout notification (Milan v1.2 Table 5.22) keeps flags 0;\n- a suite case and a planted mutant cover both;\n- the processor's suites and the parent's consumer gates pass.\n",
